msgstr ""

msgctxt "label"
msgid "Membership Categories"
msgstr ""

msgid "Select which categories are used only for membership products. This is used by other settings or to help with custom development."
msgstr ""

msgid "Touchpoints write data back from WordPress user actions back to Wicket person profiles. Configure which default touchpoint should be used."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "label"
msgid "WooCommerce Order"
msgstr ""

msgid "Enable Order touchpoint and send details to Wicket MDP."
msgstr ""

msgid "Event Tickets attendee registered for an event"
msgstr ""

msgid "Enable a touchpoint to be written when attendees register for an event. <br><small>Touchpoint is written on order complete</small>"
msgstr ""

msgid "Event Tickets attendee check-in for an event"
msgstr ""

msgid "Enable a touchpoint to be written when attendees check-in for an event"
msgstr ""

msgid "Event Tickets attendee RSVP for an event"
msgstr ""

msgid "Enable a touchpoint to be written when attendees RSVP for an event"
msgstr ""

msgid "Event Tickets attendee added by an admin or CSV import"
msgstr ""

msgid "Enable a touchpoint to be written when an attendee is added from the WordPress admin Attendees screen, or imported from CSV. Recorded as a registration, with the source noted on the touchpoint. <br><small>Imported attendees carry no registration form answers, because the CSV importer does not collect them.</small>"
msgstr ""

msgid "Event Tickets attendee removed from an event"
msgstr ""

msgid "Enable a touchpoint to be written when an attendee is removed from an event. <br><small>Written once, whether the attendee is moved to the trash or deleted outright.</small>"
msgstr ""

msgid "Include registration form answers"
msgstr ""

msgid "Include the attendee's registration form answers in event touchpoints, as label and value pairs. <br><small>Every answered field is sent. Use the wicket_tec_registration_answers filter to leave fields out.</small>"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "label"
msgid "WooCommerce"
msgstr ""

msgid "Configure settings for common customizations with default WooCommerce behaviour."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "label"
msgid "Sync Checkout Addresses"
msgstr ""

msgid "Billing and shipping addresses in WooCommerce checkout are pre-populated with the address from the Wicket person record."
msgstr ""

msgid "Remove product links from Cart & Checkout"
msgstr ""

msgid "Remove links to product pages from the cart and checkout pages"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "label"
msgid "Hide membership categories"
msgstr ""

msgid "Hide membership categories and remove from search results. Membership categories are selected in the Membership setting tab."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hide membership product single pages"
msgstr ""

msgid "Products in the categories that are identified as Membership Categories in the Wicket Settings -> Memberships Tab will have their single page redirect to the homepage. These products can still be added to cart by other methods such as the onboarding form."
msgstr ""

msgid "Remove product added to cart message"
msgstr ""

msgid "When redirected to a checkout disable the \"X added to cart, continue shopping?\" message."
msgstr ""

msgid "Block customer emails on admin updates"
msgstr ""

msgid "Stops customer emails when admins update orders unless the email is explicitly sent."
msgstr ""

msgid "Allow refund emails from admin"
msgstr ""

msgid "Allow refund emails to customers when refunds are triggered by an admin."
msgstr ""

msgid "Draft order retention (days)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Number of days a draft (checkout-draft) order is kept before being automatically deleted. Defaults to 60 days. Set to 0 to disable automatic deletion entirely. Set to 1 to match WooCommerce's built-in default behaviour. Note: this overrides WooCommerce's built-in behaviour, which deletes draft orders after just 1 day."
msgstr ""

msgid "Person to Organization Relationship Types"
msgstr ""

msgid "This is needed to determine which person to organization relationship types we want to identify that are relevant for usage on the site. One example is within WooCommerce orders."
msgstr ""

msgid "Assign people to groups on product purchase"
msgstr ""

msgid "When certain subscription products are purchased manage group assignments based on subscription dates."
msgstr ""

msgid "Group Assignment Product Category"
msgstr ""

msgid "Choose the category of product that will show the Group Assignment Tab and Settings."
msgstr ""

msgid "Group Role Entity Object Slug"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use <code>group-members</code> unless it isn't working and only if you understand why it should be different. This retrieves Group Role resource entity options from Wicket."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "label"
msgid "WP Cassify"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "label"
msgid "Sync Security Roles"
msgstr ""

msgid "Sync all roles found under profile -> security -> roles in the MDP for each user when they log in to WordPress - Requires WP-CASSIFY plugin."
msgstr ""

msgid "Sync Memberships as Roles"
msgstr ""

msgid "Sync active user memberships from the MDP for a user when they log in to WordPress. For example, if they have a membership called \"Student\" within the MDP, when they log in, a role will be created called \"Student\" if it does not yet exist and assign that role to the user. - NOTE: Requires WP-CASSIFY plugin and <strong><em> the checkbox above to be selected!</em></strong>"
msgstr ""

msgid "Sync Tags as Roles"
msgstr ""

msgid "Sync selected user tags from the MDP for a user when they log in to WordPress. Type the allowed tag(s) in this field. Values in field must match the tag in the MDP exactly. Multiple values must be comma separated."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "label"
msgid "Ignore Roles"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ignore certain user roles from the MDP for a user when they log in to WordPress. Type the allowed role(s) in this field. Values in field must match the roles in the MDP exactly. Multiple values must be comma separated. - NOTE: This only applies to security roles found on the users profile in the MDP. It does not apply to derived roles such as the ones mentioned above for memberships, etc"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "label"
msgid "Mailtrap"
msgstr ""

msgid "Used to send all WordPress mail to mailtrap. Typically used on staging/local for testing and will only take effect when the Wicket environment is toggled to \"Staging\". <br> NOTE! Remember to disable any SMTP plugin(s) while using the stage environment. Otherwise these settings won't take effect."
msgstr ""

